!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/lexer/invalid/bidi-mark-inside-unquoted-token-expected.tn"
{
  spec: "§7.1"
  description: "U+200E LEFT-TO-RIGHT MARK stands between two characters that would otherwise be one token. It is Pattern_White_Space, but UAX31-R3a-1 sorts that property into end-of-line (item 1), ignorable format controls (item 2) and horizontal space (item 3), and its own note names U+200E and U+200F as exactly item 2: they are allowed only in contexts UAX31-I1/I2/I3, 'where their insertion shall have no effect on the meaning of the program'. Reading them as horizontal space instead splits ab<LRM>c into two tokens, which is an insertion that plainly changes the meaning, and invisibly. R3a's own note gives the strategy: ignore them when lexing, then treat as illegal any lexical element that contains one. The text below is written with the literal character because that is what a reader must reject."
  outcome: error
  category: lexer
}
